course: dictionary
lesson: 2881
title: Words around us: doorbell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A doorbell is a bell or button by a front door. You press it so the people inside know you are there. «I heard the doorbell» can mean the sound it made, so the words around a word tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Ringing doorbells and running away can frighten people» shows that ringing a doorbell is something you do to someone, and that it can scare them when it is done as a prank. The sentence tells you what the doorbell does and how it can affect people.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask: is this about the button, the sound, or the house? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A doorbell is a bell or button by a front door that you press.
fact: «The doorbell rang» means the sound was heard. To «answer the doorbell» means to go to the door when it rings.
fact: Some doorbells have cameras, called video doorbells. «A doorbell camera is a common gadget, not an insult.»
fact: Many parrots copy sounds such as doorbells, so a parrot may ring like one.
fact: When you are home alone, do not open the door to someone you don't know. Check through a window, ask through the door, or do not answer.
exercise: «I heard the doorbell from the kitchen.» What does «the doorbell» mean here? | *The sound made when someone presses the bell by the front door | A kind of wild parrot | The front door itself | A cupboard in the kitchen
exercise: Ella's friend says, «Ring the doorbell once, then wait.» What should Ella do? | Knock on the window and run away | *Press the button one time and wait for an answer | Shout through the letterbox | Press it again and again until someone comes
exercise: «Ringing doorbells and running away can frighten people.» Find and copy one word that means the same as scare. | running | *frighten | away | doorbells
test: You are home alone and someone you don't know rings the doorbell. What is the safe thing to do? | Open the door wide and invite them in | *Check through a window or ask through the door, or do not answer | Tell them your address and PIN | Ring the doorbell back and run away
test: «Not everything people do is about you; a doorbell camera is a common gadget, not an insult.» What does this sentence tell you? | A doorbell camera is a rude message aimed at you | Every doorbell is broken | Doorbell cameras are only for shops | *A doorbell camera is a common gadget that many people use
exam: «Mum asked me to answer the doorbell.» What does answer the doorbell mean? | Write a letter to the bell | Ring it back as a joke | *Go to the door when it rings | Paint the bell red
